From ea1c49a8a9c9f72932fccba08af63a00755aaff6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:20:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(face): match only a face in front of the camera
 (min_face_height)

Biopass matched the largest face YOLO found, however small: a face
across the room (a few dozen pixels, scaled up to 112 for EdgeFace) or
one cut off by the frame's edge was compared like a face in front of the
screen, so a laptop unlocked for its owner walking past.

detection.min_face_height (fraction of the frame height, default 0 = no
check, as before): the largest face's box must be at least this tall
and lie wholly inside the frame, or the attempt fails (Retry) without a
match. Out of [0, 1] (or NaN) turns face off, as an out-of-range
threshold does. The debug log gives the face box, its height in the
frame and the verdict, and the best score of a failed match.

face/common/face_framing.h holds the check as a pure function; tests:
face_framing, config_validation, config_golden.
